> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based on the detailed README and changelog you provided, here is a structured summary of the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection. This project is a specialized optimization suite for **llama.cpp** targeting **AMD RDNA** GPUs (specifically RDNA3, 3.5, and 4), delivering significant performance gains, memory savings, and new model support.

### 🚀 Core Value Proposition
This is a **16-patch collection** (Block 00 + Blocks 01–15) designed to be applied on top of the `llama.cpp` fork point **`790cf51aa`**. It introduces:
*   **Performance:** RDNA-specific kernels (WMMA Flash Attention, Gated-Delta-Net), fused MoE operations, and k-quant decode paths.
*   **Memory Efficiency:** An "attention-memory campaign" (Block 15) freeing ~3.4 GiB VRAM on large models (e.g., Qwen4exp) and ~800 MiB on dense models.
*   **New Features:** Support for **Qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next)**, MTP (Multi-Token Prediction) decode, and hybrid all-reduce for multi-GPU setups.
*   **Architecture Support:** Optimized for **RDNA4** (`gfx120x`) with back-ported optimizations for **RDNA3** (`gfx1100`) and **RDNA3.5** (`gfx115x`).

---

### 📦 The 16 Blocks (Summary)

| Block | Key Feature | Details |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **00** | **Structural Fixes** | Fixes FA small-batch KV-split width invariance and Vulkan masked-V/freed-cell issues. The foundation for all other blocks. |
| **01** | **Adaptive MTP** | Adaptive draft depth (`--draft-mtp-adaptive`) for Multi-Token Prediction. |
| **02** | **Chunked GDN Prefill** | Fused chunked gated-delta-net prefill kernel (BF16/WMMA). Separate kernels for RDNA4 and RDNA3. |
| **03** | **BF16 KV Cache** | Native BF16 KV cache and Flash Attention. Includes HIP masked-V fixes. |
| **04** | **WMMA Flash-Attn** | RDNA4 WMMA Flash Attention. Also runs on RDNA3/3.5 with tuned head limits (576 for RDNA3, 320 for 3.5). |
| **05** | **CPU Bit-Identical** | Ensures CPU decode/verify batches are bit-identical. |
| **06** | **Host Buffer Revert** | Reverts host-buffer logic for discrete GPUs. |
| **07** | **Meta Device Skip** | Skips meta device wrappers. |
| **08** | **Fused Core Prefill** | Fused-core prefill kernels with GPU bit-identical results. Includes fixes for quantized KV types (`q4_1`, `q5_0`, etc.). |
| **09** | **Meta Buffer Headroom** | Adds compute-container headroom for meta buffers. |
| **10** | **k-Quant Boosts** | VDR boosts for Q4/Q5/Q6/Q8_0. Adds dedicated RDNA3.5 mmvq table. **Note:** Changes decode numerics (reordering reduction). |
| **11** | **CUDA Graph Skip** | Skips CUDA graphs for multi-token prefill (keeps them for decode). |
| **12** | **Hybrid All-Reduce** | Custom internal all-reduce for small tensors on **RDNA4 only**. Falls back to RCCL elsewhere. |
| **13** | **Fused MoE** | Fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ + mmvq short-K item-split. Validated on RDNA4, 3.5, and 3.0. |
| **14** | **Qwen4exp Support** | Full support for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (QSA sparse FA, fused indexer, MTP draft-head, WS4 hyperconn). |
| **15** | **Memory Wins** | **Major Memory Savings:** Derived KQ masks, native Q8_0/BF16 K/V in FA kernels, QSA score-chain memory optimizations. |

---

### ⚙️ Architecture & Compatibility

*   **Target Families:**
    *   **RDNA 4 (`gfx1200`/`gfx1201`):** Maximum benefit (WMMA Flash-Attn, Chunked-GDN, k-quant VDR, Block 12 All-Reduce).
    *   **RDNA 3.5 (`gfx1150`/`gfx1151`):** Strix Point/Halo APUs. Back-ported kernels with tuned limits.
    *   **RDNA 3 (`gfx1100`):** RX 7900/7800 series. Back-ported kernels.
*   **Runtime Selection:** The binary is multi-arch. It detects the device `cc`/`gcnArchName` at runtime to select the correct kernel path.
    *   *Build Example:* `GPU_TARGETS="gfx1100;gfx1151;gfx1201"`
*   **Exceptions:**
    *   **Block 12:** Internal all-reduce is **RDNA4-only**.
    *   **Block 10:** Changes decode numerics (reordering). Not bit-identical to stock builds (deterministic within build, but differs across configs).

---

### 🛠️ Installation & Workflow

**⚠️ Critical:** Do **not** use `git apply` on the concatenated series. It silently drops hunks.

1.  **Prerequisites:** A clean `llama.cpp` checkout at commit `790cf51aa`.
2.  **Apply Method:**
    *   **Recommended:** Use the provided script: `scripts/apply-all.sh` (Strict 16/16 `git am`).
    *   **Manual:** Apply patches `patches/0000-…` through `patches/0015-…` individually using `git am`.
3.  **Upstream Drift:** If upstream `llama.cpp` moves, regenerate patches using `scripts/make-patches.sh` from the forked repository.

---

### 📉 Recent Updates (as of 2026-09-13)

*   **Re-base:** Updated to upstream master `790cf51aa` (70 commits ahead of previous base).
*   **Conflict Resolution:** Resolved 4 upstream clashes regarding FA tuning, `GGML_FA_QUANTS`, MoE MMQ, and indexer V cache.
*   **Validation:**
    *   `test-backend-ops`: 18061/18061 passed.
    *   **Greedy Purity:** Plain decode matches `draft-mtp` verify for `--spec-draft-n-max <= 7`.
    *   **Memory:** Block 15 confirmed to save ~3.4 GiB/GPU on Qwen4exp.
*   **Block 13 Fixes:** Added RDNA3.5/3.0 fused-MoE-MMQ gate relaxations and fixed decode/verify band-uniformity issues.

### ⚠️ Important Caveats

1.  **Greedy Purity (Block 10):** If you require 100% bit-identical outputs across different builds/configs, **do not apply Block 10**. It reorders FP32 reductions in VDR kernels.
2.  **Block 13 Caveat:** Rewrites small-batch mmvq decode kernels. Specific fixes were applied in Sept 2026 to ensure bit-identical results for `W=1..8` on MoE projections.
3.  **Block 12 Gate:** The custom all-reduce is strictly gated to RDNA4. Multi-GPU setups on RDNA3 will fall back to RCCL.

